From 53691af5a05cd3db4941ebe647db75734b5f80bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maxjivi05 <maxjividen@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:20:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] InvalidationTracker: drop DEP promotion when a range becomes
 executable

With DEP disabled, a readable but non-executable protection (for example
PAGE_READWRITE while ntdll applies relocations) adds the range to
DEPPromotedIntervals. Restoring an executable protection afterwards did
not remove it, so the next RWX trap reprotected the range with
GetTrapProt() as PAGE_READONLY instead of PAGE_EXECUTE_READ. Relocated
32-bit DLL code then reported PAGE_READONLY to VirtualQuery and hooking
libraries refused to patch it.

Remove the range from DEPPromotedIntervals once it is given an
executable protection, matching what already happens when it loses
execute access.
---
 Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
index 64485c8a4..023691475 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
@@ -68,6 +68,8 @@ void InvalidationTracker::HandleMemoryProtectionNotification(uint64_t Address, u
       }
       if (DEPDisabled && !HasExec) {
         DEPPromotedIntervals.Insert(ProtInterval);
+      } else if (DEPDisabled) {
+        DEPPromotedIntervals.Remove(ProtInterval);
       }
       return true;
     } else if (XIntervals.Intersect(ProtInterval)) {
